  "description": "Applies a tuned production SQLite pragma set — WAL journal, `synchronous=NORMAL`, `foreign_keys=ON`, a `busy_timeout`, a shared `mmap_size` and a capped `journal_size_limit` — to every SQLite connection, so a .NET app gets correct, concurrent, production-ready SQLite by default instead of the locking-prone stock configuration. Register `AddRaskSqlite(...)` and open connections through the injected `ISqlite`; the pragmas are re-applied on every pooled connection open (the per-connection ones must be), not once at startup, and every pragma is overridable. Depends only on Microsoft.Data.Sqlite — reflection-free, so it is fine under trimming/AOT and on mobile. For Entity Framework Core's one-line `UseRaskSqlite(...)`, add the companion package Rask.SQLite.EntityFrameworkCore.",
